# /etc/crypttab — LUKS device options (idempotent, managed by
# configs/boot/luks/link.sh). Entries below are appended by the link script
# when a LUKS-encrypted root/data device is detected. Manual entries added
# above this marker are preserved across reruns.
#
# Options used (when LUKS is present):
#   luks             — detect LUKS header
#   discard          — pass TRIM/UNMAP through (matches current btrfs
#                      discard=async; tradeoff: reveals freed-block regions)
#   perf-no-read-workqueue
#   perf-no-write-workqueue
#                      — reduce dm-crypt per-bio latency on kernels ≥ 5.9;
#                      relevant on this 512e NVMe (see BOOT.md benchmarks)
#
# For auto-unlock with SB active: systemd-cryptenroll --tpm2-device auto
#   --tpm2-pcr 7 (PCR 7 binding only meaningful with Secure Boot on).
# For passphrase-based boot: mkinitcpio encrypt hook + a keyfile in the ESP,
#   or a typed passphrase prompt in the initrd.
#
# MARKER:arch-dotfiles/boot/luks — do not edit entries below this line manually
